# tsunagiya - Claude Code Rules

## Project Context
Read CLAUDE.md and REQUIREMENTS.md before starting any implementation.

## Development Workflow
1. Follow the phase order in ROADMAP.md
2. Implement one module at a time
3. Write tests alongside implementation
4. Run `deno task fmt` after each module (auto-format)
5. Run `deno task test` (all tests must pass)
6. Run `deno task check` (type-check + lint + format check)
7. Fix any errors automatically
8. Run `deno task fmt` again if manual fixes were made
9. Commit when all checks pass
10. Report phase completion to supervisor (kaniko)

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode
- No `any`, use `unknown`
- Pure functions for filters (no side effects)
- JSDoc comments for public APIs (Japanese OK)
- Error messages in English

## Testing
- Every new feature needs tests
- Use `Deno.test` for all tests
- Always call `pool.uninstall()` in `finally` blocks
- Test file naming: `*_test.ts`

## File Organization
- Core logic: `src/*.ts`
- Testing helpers: `src/testing/*.ts`
- Tests: `tests/*.ts`
- Re-export from `src/mod.ts` and `src/testing/mod.ts`

## Git Commits
- Conventional commits format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `docs:`
- Add Co-authored-by line: `Co-authored-by: kaniko (claude-code) <kaniko@openclaw.local>`

## Constraints
- Zero external dependencies (Deno std only)
- Node.js compatibility (avoid Deno-specific APIs in core logic)
- No crypto implementation (EventBuilder uses mock signatures)

## Quality Assurance (Self-Check)
After implementing each module:
1. Run `deno task fmt` - auto-format all code
2. Run `deno task test` - all tests must pass
3. Run `deno task check` - no errors allowed (type-check + lint + format check)
4. Fix any issues before moving to next module
5. Run `deno task fmt` again if any manual fixes were made
6. Commit when all checks pass

**CRITICAL:** Always run `deno task fmt` before `deno task check` to avoid format errors.
Never commit code that fails `deno task check`.

## Progress Reporting
Report to supervisor (kaniko) when:
- Completing a phase
- Encountering blocking issues
- Finishing the entire implementation

Supervisor will post updates to Discord thread.
